BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20251217T234031Z
CREATED:20251217T234031Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20251217T234031Z
DESCRIPTION:The Albanese government has been caught out again lying about their arms trade with Israel.\nDespite claims to the contrary\, an FOI request has revealed that it signed and vetted all stages of a $900 million contract with Israeli arms manufacturer Elbit Systems\, which manufactures drones used to kill Palestinians in Gaza.\nSeeking to divert attention from its complicity with Israel’s Gaza genocide\, the Albanese government has backed a report by arch Zionist and antisemitism envoy Jillian Segal that proposed a widespread crackdown on protests opposing Israel’s Gaza genocide.\nThe Special Envoy’s Plan to Combat Antisemitism proposes that all levels of government adopt the widely discredited IHRA definition of antisemitism\, which has been used to silence legitimate criticism of Israel and Zionism.\nIt advocates surveillance\, censorship\, and punitive control over the funding of cultural and educational institutions: measures straight out of Trump’s authoritarian playbook.\nWe call on the Australian government to:\n– repudiate the Special Envoy’s Plan\n– sack Jillian Segal\n– implement sanctions on Israel\, including a comprehensive arms embargo.
DTEND:20250802T060000Z
LOCATION:Forrest Place\nForrest Pl\, Perth WA 6000
DTSTART:20250802T040000Z
SUMMARY:We will not be silenced! End the genocide!
UID:fcef3e27-a682-43a2-90ba-59eed0a16e86@boorloo-actionpulse.org
URL:https://fopwa.org/events/we-will-not-be-silenced-end-the-genocide/
END:VEVENT

BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20251217T234031Z
CREATED:20251217T234031Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20251217T234031Z
DESCRIPTION:Israel’s ongoing blockade of Gaza has created a devastating hunger crisis\, putting over 320\,000 children at risk of acute malnutrition and leaving 40\,000 infants at risk of imminent death.\nThe deliberate starvation of 2.3 million people has pushed the Strip to the brink of collapse.\nDespite mounting public pressure\, the Australian government has failed to take meaningful action.\nOur government continues to allow shipments of military supplies to Israel\, including a shipment of F-35 parts just last month\, and has not imposed sanctions despite the clear violations of international law and perpetration of war crimes.\nFollowing the massive March for Humanity across the Sydney Harbour Bridge on August 3\, Palestine solidarity groups across Australia have called for a nationwide march on August 24.\nThe rallies are demanding an end to the starvation and genocide\, and are calling on the Australian government to impose sanctions on Israel and enforce a two-way arms embargo.\nJoin us in Perth on Sunday August 24\, 12 noon at Forrest Place. We will hear from speakers and march at 1pm to Hyde Park.
DTEND:20250824T060000Z
LOCATION:Forrest Place\nForrest Pl\, Perth WA 6000
DTSTART:20250824T040000Z
SUMMARY:National March for Palestine (Perth): Save Gaza\, Sanctions Now!
UID:82566517-a882-4924-808c-d6bd0c1cb5be@boorloo-actionpulse.org
URL:https://fopwa.org/events/national-march-for-palestine-perth-save-gaza-sanctions-now/
END:VEVENT

